### Demon { #mythic-demon }

#### Mythic Rank 3 { #demon-m3 }

The Demon gains Demonic Rage, initially usable three times per day, with each use lasting for one combat.

For Cave Fangs, Demonic Rage provides +2 DC to both the Cave Fangs buff and the traps themselves. One use can be spent in a minor encounter to cast the buff, retaining the +2 DC bonus for the rest of the dungeon. This leaves two uses available for important encounters, where another +2 DC can be gained, for a total of +4 DC during Rage.

??? demon-feature "Demonic Rage"
    {% include '_includes/demonic_rage.md' %}

#### Mythic Rank 4 { #demon-m4 }

The Demon gains a minor Demon Aspect.

**Brimorak** appears to offer additional damage, but its bonus only applies to Fire spells and therefore does not benefit Stalactite Traps.

??? demon-feature "Aspect of Brimorak"
    {% include '_includes/aspect_brimorak.md' %}

**Incubus** provides another +1 DC during Demonic Rage.

??? demon-feature "Aspect of Incubus"
    {% include '_includes/aspect_incubus.md' %}

**Babau**, the alternative, provides additional sneak attack damage, which benefits Surprise Spells.

??? demon-feature "Aspect of Babau"
    {% include '_includes/aspect_babau.md' %}

#### Mythic Rank 5 {demon-m5}

At Mythic Rank 5, the Demon gains another minor Aspect and two major Aspects. Two minor Aspects can now be active simultaneously.

??? demon-feature "Extra Minor Aspect"
    {% include '_includes/demon_extra_minor_aspect.md' %}

**Vrock** imposes a –1 penalty to enemy Reflex saves. 

??? demon-feature "Aspect of Vrock"
    {% include '_includes/aspect_vrock.md' %}

Two major Aspects provide bonuses to the casting ability score, and therefore to DC:

- **Shadow Demon** increases Wisdom.
- **Coloxus** increases Intelligence.

These ability score bonuses are passive.

??? demon-feature "Aspect of Shadow Demon"
    {% include '_includes/aspect_shadow_demon.md' %}

??? demon-feature "Aspect of Coloxus"
    {% include '_includes/aspect_coloxus.md' %}

At this stage, the additional benefit is +1 DC (or +2 DC with uneven casting ability score).

No other major Aspects provide relevant synergy with Cave Fangs.

#### Mythic Rank 6 { #demon-m6 }

Demonic Rage increases to four uses per day. Most Aspect benefits also improve.

The additional minor Aspects provide no further benefits relevant to Cave Fangs.

Incubus is always used for the buffing encounter. 

For major encounters, the choice is between Incubus and Vrock for higher DC, or Babau and Vrock for additional sneak attack damage if using Suprise Spells.

| Configuration | Buff DC | Effective Trap DC | Suprise Spells |
|---|---:|---:| ---- :|
| Incubus + Any -> Incubus + Vrock | +7 | +14 | |
| Incubus + Any -> Babau + Vrock | +7 | +12 | +3d6|

#### Mythic Rank 9 { #demon-m9 }

Demonic Rage increases to five uses per day. Most Aspect benefits improve again.

| Configuration | Buff DC | Effective Trap DC | Suprise Spells |
|---|---:|---:| ---- :|
| Incubus + Any -> Incubus + Vrock | +9 | +19 | |
| Incubus + Any -> Babau + Vrock | +9 | +16 | +4d6|

The Demon also gains access to a Demon Lord Aspect.
{: #demon-deskari }

**Deskari** allows the Demon to bypass physical damage immunity.

??? demon-feature "Aspect of Deskari"
    {% include '_includes/aspect_of_deskari.md' %}

#### Mythic Rank 10

+1 DC from Coloxus or Shadow Demon.


#### Discussion

The Demon offers the highest trap DC of the mythic paths discussed here, alongside additional sneak attack damage for Surprise Spells builds.

The main limitation is the lack of damage conversion. Deskari provides a way to bypass physical damage immunity, but only at Mythic Rank 9.
</file>

<file path="_includes/mythic_gold_dragon.md">
### Gold Dragon { #mythic-gd }

The Gold Dragon loses all mythic features belonging to the previous path.

The exception is a merged spellbook (Angel and Lich). An unmerged mythic spellbook is lost.

#### Mythic 8 

Perfect Body's additional damage applies to Stalactite Traps and the sneak attack damage from Surprise Spells (link to be added).

??? gd-feature "Perfect Body"
    {% include '_includes/gold_dragon_perfect_body.md' %}

The Gold Dragon gains Dragon Breath, a useful standard-action option for use alongside the free-action traps. By itself it gives a -1 DC debuff on a save and -3 DC on a fail.

??? gd-feature "Dragon Breath"
    {% include '_includes/gold_dragon_gold_dragon_breath.md' %}

The Mind-Clearing Breath upgrade can be combined with Dispel Synergy for another -2 DC.

??? feat "Dispel Synergy"
    {% include '_includes/dispel_synergy.md' %}

??? gd-feature "Mind-Clearing Breath"
    {% include '_includes/gold_dragon_mind_clearing_breath.md' %}

The Gold Dragon also gains two strong spells at Mythic Rank 8.

Dragon Might increases all damage dealt by 50%. This applies to traps, Geomancy, and the sneak attack damage from Surprise Spells.
    
??? spell "Dragon Might"
    {% include '_includes/gold_dragon_dragon_might.md' %}

Dragon Smite's flat damage bonus applies to Geomancy and traps.

??? spell "Dragon Smite"
    {% include '_includes/gold_dragon_dragon_smite.md' %}

#### Mythic 9

Perfect Mind increases damage slightly compared with Perfect Body. More importantly, it provides unlimited Holy damage conversion.

??? gd-feature "Perfect Mind"
    {% include '_includes/gold_dragon_perfect_mind.md' %}

This leaves a gap in damage conversion between Mythic Ranks 8 and 9. However, Mythic Rank 9 may be reachable with very little combat, if the information I read is correct.

The Gold Dragon also gains another Dragon Breath upgrade.

Overwhelming Breath to increase the chance enemies fail their reflex save is a good choice.
Both for damage and the extra -2 DC debuff.

??? gd-feature "Overwhelming Breath"
    {% include '_includes/gold_dragon_overwhelming_breath.md' %}
    

#### Mythic 10 { #gd-m10 }

With Perfect Soul, damage dice become d10s. This applies to both the regular trap damage and Surprise Spells. In addition, spells (and abilities) are automatically Empowered and Maximised, this includes the traps (but not the sneak attack), Geomancy and even [Call of the Fiery Things](#fire-items) procs.

For traps, this removes the need to use Plague of Madness. The greater benefit is to Geomancy, which is also Empowered and Maximised. A standard Geomancy proc now deals:

9 × 6 × 1.5 = 81 damage

The Empower effect also applies to additional flat damage riders on Geomancy, such as Dragon Smite or an allied Paladin's Mark of Justice.

??? gd-feature "Perfect Soul"
    {% include '_includes/gold_dragon_perfect_soul.md' %}

The Gold dragon also gets three Dragon Feats.

??? gd-feature "Dragon Feat"
    {% include '_includes/gold_dragon_dragon_feat.md' %}

Some recommendations:

Grand Cognatogen provides a +8 bonus to one mental ability score, +6 to another and +4 to a third. It is particularly useful with Dragon Smite. If the casting ability is not Charisma, Charisma can be selected as the second ability score for a +6 bonus.

??? class-feature "Grand Cognatogen"
    {% include '_includes/grand_cognatogen.md' %}

At least one level of Alchemist or Mutation Warrior is required to use the ability. Vivisectionist may also provide the prerequisite Sneak Dice for the Arcane Trickster prestige class (link to be added), making it a potential choice for builds focused on Surprise Spells.

Extra Magus Arcana: Reach Magic is a useful for extending trap placement range, particularly against spread-out enemies.

??? class-feature "Reach Magic"
    {% include '_includes/magus_arcana_reach_magic.md' %}

Flame Curse is not recommended. Dragon Breath already provides a strong standard-action option.

Flame Curse is only better in a theoretical scenario with a single enemy with a higher HP value then any enemy in the game has. 

Otherwise Flame Curse requires a substantial amount of additional flat damage on traps to be worthwhile compared with Dragon Breath. This means having Hellknight levels, an allied Paladin's Mark of Justice and Dragon Smite.

However quickening Dragon Smite through Boots of Arcane Persistence conflicts with Dragon Might, as both spells require a swift action. 

??? item "Boots of Arcane Persistence"
    {% include '_includes/boots_of_arcane_persistence.md' %}

Flame Curse can also be cast by an ally.

The Gold Dragon also gains two further Dragon Breath upgrades.

#### Discussion

The Gold Dragon has the highest damage ceiling for a Cave Fangs build.

Perfect Soul also changes the sneak attack dice from Surprise Spells to d10s, making the Gold Dragon particularly effective for an Arcane Trickster build.

It is arguably the strongest continuation for an Arcane Trickster Lich build, as the Lich offers fewer options for increasing Cave Fangs damage at higher Mythic Ranks.

The Angel already has very high damage potential, so switching to the Gold Dragon offers less of an advantage.

Dragon Smite is not essential to the build and competes with Dragon Might for spell slots. This also means that the build does not need to be Charisma-based.
</file>

